  "title": "The Reused Key Opens Too Many Doors",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "consumer digital literacy",
  "premise": "An account owner wants one compromised fictional account to stay an isolated problem, but a reused password is represented by one key fitting several doors. Distinct symbolic credentials separate the doors in the reviewed security lesson.",
